// Using the source "one_helpful.md" as the base content, create a plantuml activity diagram to represent any
// workflows, processes, or sequence of actions described in the document. Focus on key steps, decisions, and parallel activities.


@startuml
title Workflow for Cultivating Heedfulness & Skillful Qualities

start

group Initial State
  :Experience Stress & Suffering;
  note right
    This state is characterized by being "beset by birth, aging, & death; by sorrows, lamentations, pains, distresses, & despairs; beset by stress, overcome with stress" [AN_nblm.txt, 14, 15].
  end note
  :Do you desire to end suffering?;
end group

if (Desire to end suffering?) then (Yes)
  group Cultivation Process
    partition "Foundation: Cultivating Heedfulness (Appamada)" {
      :**Cultivate Heedfulness**;
      note right
        **Heedfulness (Appamada)** is described as a single quality that guards the mind and is reckoned as the foremost among all skillful qualities [AN_nblm.txt, 175, 176][KN_Iti_nblm.txt, 306][SN_nblm.txt, 502]. It involves being **attentive** and **resolute**, and cherishing it as one's highest wealth [AN_nblm.txt, 54][MN_nblm.txt, 393][KN_Dhp_nblm.txt, 302].

        **Conditions for Heedfulness**:
        *   **Shame and compunction** precede clear knowing [KN_Iti_nblm.txt, 310][SN_nblm.txt, 568].
        *   **Clear knowing** precedes shame and compunction [SN_nblm.txt, 568].
        *   **Guarding the mind** with regard to effluents [SN_nblm.txt, 598].
        *   Developing mindfulness of death acutely for the sake of ending effluents [AN_nblm.txt, 111, 112].
      end note

      fork
        :Abandon Bodily Misconduct;
        :Abandon Verbal Misconduct;
        :Abandon Mental Misconduct;
        :Abandon Wrong View;
      fork again
        :Develop Good Bodily Conduct;
        :Develop Good Verbal Conduct;
        :Develop Good Mental Conduct;
        :Develop Right View;
      end fork
      note right
        Heedfulness requires abandoning misconduct and developing good conduct in these areas [AN_nblm.txt, 54, 55, 618].
      end note

      :Guard mind from passion, aversion, delusion, intoxication;
      :Be mindful & alert in all daily activities (e.g., walking, standing, eating);
      :Pursue mindfulness of in-&-out breathing;
      :Live ardently & resolutely for ending effluents;
      note right
        Heedfulness encompasses guarding mind-states, mindfulness in daily life, and a resolute pursuit of liberation [AN_nblm.txt, 55, 114][MN_nblm.txt, 380, 392, 394, 404, 455, 480][SN_nblm.txt, 552, 601][KN_Iti_nblm.txt, 309].
      end note
    }

    partition "Development: Cultivating Skillful Qualities" {
      :**Cultivate Skillful Qualities**;
      note right
        **Skillful qualities** are mental qualities and actions that lead to welfare and happiness, are blameless, and are praised by observant people [AN_nblm.txt, 2, 27, 614].

        **Roots of Skillful Qualities**:
        *   **Lack of greed**
        *   **Lack of aversion**
        *   **Lack of delusion** [AN_nblm.txt, 32][DN_nblm.txt, 241][MN_nblm.txt, 353, 617]

        **Conditions for Skillful Qualities**:
        *   **Clear knowing** [KN_Iti_nblm.txt, 310][SN_nblm.txt, 568].
        *   **Associating with people of integrity**, hearing the True Dhamma, appropriate attention, and practicing the Dhamma [DN_nblm.txt, 244][SN_nblm.txt, 607].
        *   **Conviction** in the Teacher's message, leading to hearing, remembering, penetrating meaning, pondering, desire, willingness, contemplation, and exertion [MN_nblm.txt, 430, 454].
        *   **Tranquility (samatha)** and **insight (vipassanā)**, which help abandon passion and ignorance respectively [AN_nblm.txt, 3][DN_nblm.txt, 269][SN_nblm.txt, 565, 566].
      end note

      fork
        :Practice Skillful Bodily Action (e.g., abstaining from taking life, stealing, sexual misconduct);
        :Practice Skillful Verbal Action (e.g., abstaining from lying, divisive/harsh speech, idle chatter);
        :Practice Skillful Mental Action (e.g., non-covetousness, goodwill, right view);
      fork again
        :Develop Heightened Virtue (e.g., dwelling restrained by Pāṭimokkha rules);
        :Develop Heightened Concentration (Jhāna) (e.g., secluded from sensuality, entering meditative absorptions);
        :Develop Heightened Discernment (e.g., understanding arising/passing away, investigating truths);
      fork again
        :Develop Mindfulness (e.g., the four establishings of mindfulness, in-&-out breathing);
        :Address Defilements (e.g., contemplation of unattractiveness for lust, goodwill for ill will);
        :Engage in Community & Learning (e.g., associating with admirable friends, listening to/discussing Dhamma);
      fork again
        :Practice Generosity (e.g., being freely generous, openhanded);
        :Maintain Aroused Persistence (e.g., steadfast effort to abandon unskillful & take on skillful);
      end fork
      note right
        The cultivation of skillful qualities involves a wide range of interconnected practices across conduct, mental states, and learning [1].
      end note
    }
  end group

  group Outcome: End of Suffering
    :Experience Decline in Unskillful Qualities;
    :Experience Increase in Skillful Qualities;
    note left
      This directly results from cultivating skillful qualities [AN_nblm.txt, 36, 615].
    end note

    :Attain purity of mind, calm, & joy;
    :Develop discernment & abandon ignorance;
    :Abandon passion, aversion, & delusion;

    :Achieve **Awareness-Release**;
    :Achieve **Discernment-Release**;
    note right
      This is the "liberation of the mind through lack of clinging or sustenance" [MN_nblm.txt, 421].
      It is enabled by abandoning passion and ignorance [AN_nblm.txt, 4][DN_nblm.txt, 239].
    end note

    :Realize **Unbinding** (Nibbana);
    note right
      Marked by the understanding that "Birth is ended, the holy life fulfilled, the task done. There is nothing further for this world." [MN_nblm.txt, 354].
    end note

    :Experience the **Ending of Craving**;
    :Experience the **Ending of Suffering & Stress**;
    note right
      "From the ending of craving is the cessation of stress" [AN_nblm.txt, 88][KN_Dhp_nblm.txt, 305].
      This process leads to the purification of beings, overcoming sorrow, and realizing unbinding [DN_nblm.txt, 222][AN_nblm.txt, 61].
    end note
  end group
else (No)
  :Continue experiencing Stress & Suffering;
endif

stop
@enduml